## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, beginner-friendly security planning around vendor integrations, token binding, and incident response in a multi-tenant setup.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation
- Audience-bound tokens
- API gateway introspection
- Secrets scanning in CI
- IR playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// sample token audience check
function authorize(token, audience, tenantId){
  const payload = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, { audience });
  if (payload.tenant_id !== tenantId) throw new Error('Tenant mismatch');
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate per-tenant API keys and verify their use in logs?
- What metrics indicate cross-tenant access was prevented?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate data-security policy into concrete export controls.

## Key Concepts
- Data minimization and redaction
- RBAC and per-session scopes
- Token-based session gating
- Centralized exporting logs and retention
- IR playbooks and containment steps

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express route sketch: enforce role-based redaction on export
app.post('/exports/statements', authorize(['viewer','exporter']), (req,res)=>{
  const fields = req.user.role==='exporter' ? fullFields : ['date','amount','balance'];
  const csv = generateCSV(data, fields);
  res.setHeader('Content-Type','text/csv');
  res.send(csv);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the export redaction in CI?
- What metrics indicate success of the control?
